Which license applies to what
-----------------------------

1. Software – PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0
   SPDX-License-Identifier: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
   Full text: LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md
   Applies to: firmware/, web/, hardware/scripts/, tools/ (where created by
   this project), justfile, setup.sh and any other source code in this
   repository.

   Required Notice: Copyright 2026 Christian Ditscher (https://github.com/ditschi/looping_louie)

2. Hardware designs and documentation – Creative Commons
   Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
   SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
   Full text: LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt
   Applies to: hardware/ (KiCad projects, schematics, layouts, BOM, own
   symbols/footprints/3D models, mechanical parts) except hardware/scripts/,
   docs/, README.md and images.

   Attribution: "Looping Louie WLAN upgrade by Christian Ditscher,
   https://github.com/ditschi/looping_louie"

Third-party material
--------------------

Files from third parties keep their own licenses, in particular:
- hardware/lib/lcsc.* – symbols, footprints and 3D models converted from
  LCSC/EasyEDA with easyeda2kicad (terms of LCSC/EasyEDA apply).
- KiCad standard library parts referenced by the projects (CC-BY-SA 4.0 with
  the KiCad library exception).
- Rust crates, ESP-IDF and other dependencies (their respective licenses,
  mostly MIT/Apache-2.0); they are not covered by the licenses above.

Earlier versions
----------------

Versions before this file was added (including the tag v1-legacy) were
published without a license; all rights reserved for those versions unless
stated otherwise.

Contributions
-------------

By submitting a contribution (pull request, patch) you agree that it is
licensed under the terms above and that the copyright holder may additionally
license it under other terms, including commercial licenses.
